  "result": "I haven't edited any code, because plan mode is on. The plan is written to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-vivid-glacier.md`. I have no ExitPlanMode tool in this session, so I can't submit it for formal approval. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the changes.\n\n**Cause:** all four shells (bash, zsh, fish, PowerShell) split the typed command line with `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` (around lines 603-635). That function uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. For example, `cli a #b c` comes back as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`, so the `#b` word and everything after it are lost. Fish can also crash with an `IndexError` on a bare `#`.\n\n**Fix:**\n1. **Code:** in `split_arg_string`, add `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True`.\n2. **Tests:** add `#` cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py` and to `test_full_complete` in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`.\n3. **Changelog:** add an entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n\nTo verify, I'd run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, then the full suite, then `ruff`.",
